## Hints (ordered)

- A: CAGR uses the geometric mean — compound the whole sample, then take the
  1/n_years root.
- B1: `np.log1p(r).resample("W-FRI").sum()` vs `np.log(P_fri / P_last_fri)`.
- B2: near zero, ln(1+r) ≈ r − r²/2; the divergence grows quadratically.
